From: Brick firmware maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] input: keep the built-in Menu key as a recovery exit

The external controller is Player 1 while connected, but the permanently
available built-in controls must still be able to return to the product shell.
RetroArch normally reads meta hotkeys only from the hotkey port. Promote the
built-in controller's autoconfig Menu event to Quit after input collection so
this recovery path remains independent of player assignment.

---
 input/input_driver.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/input/input_driver.c b/input/input_driver.c
index beba85e..a9af15e 100644
--- a/input/input_driver.c
+++ b/input/input_driver.c
@@ -6913,6 +6913,16 @@ void input_driver_collect_system_input(input_driver_state_t *input_st,
             &joypad_info,
             settings->bools.input_hotkey_device_merge);
 
+      /* Product recovery control: this physical pad is always present even
+       * when an external controller owns Player 1. */
+      if (string_is_equal(input_config_get_device_name(joypad_info.joy_idx),
+                          "TrimUI Brick Gamepad") &&
+          BIT256_GET_PTR(current_bits, RARCH_MENU_TOGGLE))
+      {
+         BIT256_CLEAR_PTR(current_bits, RARCH_MENU_TOGGLE);
+         BIT256_SET_PTR(current_bits, RARCH_QUIT_KEY);
+      }
+
 #ifdef HAVE_MENU
       if (menu_is_alive)
       {
-- 
